# Deny everything, then allow only what the build actually needs.
#
# Without this, the build context includes the ~8GB ISE tar, the whole
# private/ directory and .git -- all uploaded to the daemon on every build.
#
# The ISE tar stays whitelisted for INSTALL_METHOD=bind, whose
# RUN --mount=type=bind,src= resolves its source in the build context.
# BuildKit only transfers the paths a build uses, so with INSTALL_METHOD=http
# the tar is never sent. With bind it is copied into the BuildKit cache.
*

!Xilinx_ISE_DS_14.7_1015_1.tar
!Xilinx.lic
!headless-install.conf
!firmware-load.sh
!usb-driver

usb-driver/.git
